Yeah, hello?

5
00:00:46,833 --> 00:00:48,267
I just got here.

6
00:00:48,267 --> 00:00:51,600
What floor was it again?
Has forensics arrived?

7
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:44,400
- You're here?
- Yeah.

8
00:01:50,467 --> 00:01:54,367
The bullet went straight through his temple.
Death was instantaneous.

9
00:01:54,367 --> 00:01:56,200
Have you identified the victim?

10
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:57,467
Yeah.

11
00:01:57,467 --> 00:02:00,167
But, wow... I've never seen
anything like this.

12
00:02:00,167 --> 00:02:03,648
Wow, this is unbelievable.
A gun murder in South Korea?

13
00:02:03,648 --> 00:02:06,833
So I've been thinking,
could this possibly be...

14
00:02:06,833 --> 00:02:08,400
The victim's identity?

15
00:02:10,944 --> 00:02:12,467
Sir, here it is.

16
00:02:14,033 --> 00:02:16,700
Hwang Min Ho, 38 years old.

17
00:02:16,700 --> 00:02:18,350
The interesting thing is that
he was just released

18
00:02:18,350 --> 00:02:19,800
after serving time for murder.

19
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:23,100
He staged his pregnant wife's death
and collected the insurance.

20
00:02:23,100 --> 00:02:25,300
He served three years
and got out three days ago.

21
00:02:25,300 --> 00:02:29,200
Just three years?
That's all he got for murder?

22
00:02:30,267 --> 00:02:31,733
It was ruled as a drunk driving case.

23
00:02:31,733 --> 00:02:34,367
His wife, who was
in the passenger seat, died.

24
00:02:34,367 --> 00:02:36,608
They could never prove
it was a planned accident,

25
00:02:36,608 --> 00:02:38,784
so he only got vehicular homicide.

26
00:02:38,784 --> 00:02:41,867
So, I've been thinking, could this be...

27
00:02:41,867 --> 00:02:43,833
Estimated time of death?

28
00:02:45,467 --> 00:02:49,333
According to the coroner, it appears that
at least 12 hours have passed.

29
00:02:49,333 --> 00:02:51,067
He had a 4 a.m. wake-up call request,

30
00:02:51,067 --> 00:02:52,833
but he didn't answer, so a staff member
went up and found him.

31
00:02:52,833 --> 00:02:55,433
He had a ticket to the Philippines,

32
00:02:55,433 --> 00:02:57,167
so he was probably planning
to catch the first flight out.

33
00:02:57,167 --> 00:03:00,733
Looks like he was taking the money
and running overseas to start a new life.

34
00:03:00,733 --> 00:03:02,267
12 hours?

35
00:03:03,167 --> 00:03:05,400
So that would've been yesterday afternoon?

36
00:03:18,033 --> 00:03:20,800
The window was still open
when the staff member arrived.

37
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:22,933
Clearly a chain-smoker.

38
00:03:23,867 --> 00:03:27,333
Wow... Where on earth
did the bullet come from?

39
00:03:28,167 --> 00:03:30,633
Sir! I found this!

40
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:34,767
It's a bullet!
Wow, a bullet is lodged in here.

41
00:03:34,767 --> 00:03:35,833
A real one-shot, one-kill...

42
00:03:35,833 --> 00:03:37,633
- Keep it down.
- Yes, sir.

43
00:04:21,367 --> 00:04:23,200
No, no way...

44
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:27,200
Even so, that's way too far...

45
00:05:14,633 --> 00:05:17,133
What are you doing? What's going on?

46
00:05:17,133 --> 00:05:18,733
I know you're the police,

47
00:05:18,733 --> 00:05:20,700
