A sniper shot from 500 meters away?

246
00:16:14,200 --> 00:16:16,200
I mean, besides that guy...

247
00:16:16,200 --> 00:16:19,500
That punk was quiet for four years.

248
00:16:19,500 --> 00:16:23,567
Why now, all of a sudden?
And why our district of all places?

249
00:16:23,567 --> 00:16:25,000
No need for a long explanation.

250
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:27,133
Can you catch him or not?

251
00:16:27,133 --> 00:16:28,667
We'll investigate.

252
00:16:28,667 --> 00:16:30,700
Good. If you're going to catch him,
do it quickly.

253
00:16:30,700 --> 00:16:33,300
If it looks impossible,
wrap it up quietly when the time is right.

254
00:16:33,300 --> 00:16:35,667
Don't make a big scene for no reason.

255
00:16:35,667 --> 00:16:39,000
The higher-ups aren't expecting much anyway.

256
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:42,467
People considered the best of the best
couldn't catch him for 16 years in 93 tries.

257
00:16:42,467 --> 00:16:44,767
What makes us any different?

258
00:16:45,800 --> 00:16:51,267
Even you, the ace of Violent Crimes,
couldn't catch him once.

259
00:16:56,133 --> 00:17:00,600
If we just drag our feet, he'll probably
move on somewhere else soon.

260
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:02,233
Just until then...

261
00:17:03,567 --> 00:17:05,233
Hey, I'm talking to you.

262
00:17:05,233 --> 00:17:08,800
Hey, you handle the briefing too.
Just wing it.

263
00:17:14,767 --> 00:17:16,733
[Violent Crimes Team 1]

264
00:17:16,733 --> 00:17:18,800
- You're here.
- Yeah.

265
00:17:24,633 --> 00:17:26,133
What are you doing?

266
00:17:27,533 --> 00:17:31,300
I was curious why he's called Kingfisher,
so I looked it up.

267
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:34,267
Wow, it just means "kingfisher" in Korean.

268
00:17:34,267 --> 00:17:36,633
I seriously thought it was the kind of bird
that shoots water guns or something.

269
00:17:36,633 --> 00:17:41,200
But apparently, its beak is long
and shaped almost like a sniper rifle.

270
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:42,592
It perches way up high.

271
00:17:42,592 --> 00:17:46,333
The moment it spots prey,
it shoots into the water like a bullet...

272
00:17:46,333 --> 00:17:48,000
Are you out of your mind?

273
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:50,467
Is this really the time for you
to be wasting time on this nonsense?

274
00:17:53,567 --> 00:17:58,000
I checked the CCTV center.
Just as we thought, all footage was erased.

275
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:00,967
The witnesses inside the church
were in choir practice at the time,

276
00:18:00,967 --> 00:18:03,200
so they were all gathered in the main hall
and didn't see anything.

277
00:18:03,200 --> 00:18:06,933
The singing was so loud
that they didn't hear anything either.

278
00:18:06,933 --> 00:18:08,300
Choir?

279
00:18:08,300 --> 00:18:10,667
What about the people who drove,
the ones with dashcams?

280
00:18:10,667 --> 00:18:12,633
I already asked about that.

281
00:18:12,633 --> 00:18:15,267
There were seven people
who drove to the church that day.

282
00:18:15,267 --> 00:18:17,792
But the above-ground parking lot
was closed off,

283
00:18:17,792 --> 00:18:19,667
so they all parked underground.

284
00:18:19,667 --> 00:18:24,667
But the church says they never
blocked the above-ground parking lot.

285
00:18:24,667 --> 00:18:28,833
Of course, they didn't.
Someone else must have.

286
00:18:28,833 --> 00:18:30,233
Yeah, someone else...

287
00:18:30,233 --> 00:18:33,133
What? What do you mean, someone else?

288
00:18:36,033 --> 00:18:37,533
- Come with me.
- What?

289
00:18:38,233 --> 00:18:42,033
Study all the Kingfisher
case files by tomorrow.

290
00:18:42,033 --> 00:18:43,967
Memorize every single detail.

291
00:18:45,300 --> 00:18:47,200
Got it?

292
00:18:47,200 --> 00:18:49,000
Wait, all this in one day?

293
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:50,900
This isn't even cramming for an exam.

294
00:18:50,900 --> 00:18:52,000
I'll test you.

295
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:53,567
Yes, sir!

296
00:18:53,567 --> 00:18:55,167
Good luck.

297
00:18:59,367 --> 00:19:02,033
[The Kingfisher Case Files]

298
00:19:03,433 --> 00:19:06,467
When did he even collect all of this?

299
00:19:06,467 --> 00:19:07,552
[About Kingfisher,]
Sniper attacks

300
00:19:07,552 --> 00:19:09,600
[are we not catching him,]
are one of the most difficult crimes

301
00:19:09,600 --> 00:19:12,033
[or can we not catch him?]
to investigate and solve.

302
00:19:12,033 --> 00:19:14,976
There are usually no clues
left behind at the crime scene,

303
00:19:14,976 --> 00:19:17,333
such as fingerprints, footprints, or DNA.

304
00:19:17,333 --> 00:19:21,800
It's also extremely difficult to determine
where the shot was fired from.

305
00:19:21,800 --> 00:19:23,833
And even if we take the time to find it,

306
00:19:23,833 --> 00:19:26,967
any traces that may have been
left at the sniper's position

307
00:19:26,967 --> 00:19:28,467
will already be gone.

308
00:19:28,467 --> 00:19:30,800
It's been a long time
since I've seen this on the news.

309
00:19:30,800 --> 00:19:33,767
It'll probably be all over the news for days.

310
00:19:33,767 --> 00:19:37,033
By the way, everything's okay, right?

311
00:19:37,933 --> 00:19:40,967
You know what Bo Na's like. Don't worry.

312
00:19:40,967 --> 00:19:45,433
Well, I'm not worried or anything,
but... why was her leg shaking?

313
00:19:47,100 --> 00:19:48,600
What about you, Team Leader?

314
00:19:48,600 --> 00:19:53,200
Hey, my leg wasn't shaking.
It just cramped up for a second.

315
00:19:57,367 --> 00:20:01,833
Fine. Honestly, as the team leader,
I was a little concerned.

316
00:20:01,833 --> 00:20:04,400
It's been four years
since Director Yoo had her baby.

317
00:20:04,400 --> 00:20:08,967
Even athletes worry that they won't be
the same after taking just a year off.

318
00:20:08,967 --> 00:20:14,900
I wondered if she might be getting tired
or feeling nervous...

319
00:20:14,900 --> 00:20:17,967
What if she made a mistake?

320
00:20:17,967 --> 00:20:19,800
She said it gave her chills.

321
00:20:21,767 --> 00:20:23,433
Chills?

322
00:20:23,433 --> 00:20:24,833
It was creepy too.

323
00:20:24,833 --> 00:20:26,800
The great Yoo Bo Na?

324
00:20:30,900 --> 00:20:35,467
Wow, this place really hasn't changed.

325
00:20:35,467 --> 00:20:38,667
How do you even breathe, eat, and sleep here?

326
00:20:38,667 --> 00:20:42,000
When was your last health checkup?
Do you ever even go home?

327
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:45,667
You're here? That was quite a greeting.

328
00:20:45,667 --> 00:20:49,667
Pulled another all-nighter, huh?
What were you tinkering with all night?

329
00:20:49,667 --> 00:20:54,633
The boss wanted me to make something
flow smoothly, like this and that.

330
00:20:54,633 --> 00:20:59,033
So I made it, but I was looking for
one more source.

331
00:20:59,033 --> 00:21:00,467
Oh, really?

332
00:21:00,467 --> 00:21:03,167
So I played around with it
like this and that.

333
00:21:03,167 --> 00:21:06,133
And turns out it's a flying fly.
The fly just kind of...

334
00:21:14,167 --> 00:21:15,833
You changed your gear a bit?

335
00:21:15,833 --> 00:21:20,333
Oh, you noticed? That's Yoo Bo Na for you.

336
00:21:23,200 --> 00:21:27,967
It's a bit lighter and has less vibration.

337
00:21:27,967 --> 00:21:30,833
The ammunition must have changed too.

338
00:21:30,833 --> 00:21:33,167
It's fine. It only took a few months.

339
00:21:33,167 --> 00:21:35,633
- Do you like it?
- Yeah.

340
00:21:35,633 --> 00:21:37,067
Thanks to you, it was much better.

341
00:21:37,067 --> 00:21:41,200
My kid has grown so much lately.
She's 16 kilograms now.

342
00:21:41,200 --> 00:21:43,200
My gift for your comeback.

343
00:21:55,900 --> 00:22:00,833
Yes, Miss! What? What is it?

344
00:22:00,833 --> 00:22:02,367
What?

345
00:22:11,167 --> 00:22:14,633
Wait, you mean what made Director Yoo nervous
was because of her child?

346
00:22:16,067 --> 00:22:19,600
Yul sleeps well, and this morning...

347
00:22:19,600 --> 00:22:23,667
Was Director Yoo in there?
Without even wearing a mask?

348
00:22:23,667 --> 00:22:26,567
Could you let me video call her?
I'll try talking to her.

349
00:22:26,567 --> 00:22:28,733
Yeah, I'll set it up.

350
00:22:30,767 --> 00:22:32,333
Yul!

351
00:22:33,100 --> 00:22:37,400
Oh, my Yul! Why don't you want to take a nap?

352
00:22:37,400 --> 00:22:39,700
All your friends are sleeping. Why don't you?

353
00:22:39,700 --> 00:22:42,700
A monster appeared in my dream,
and I'm scared.

354
00:22:42,700 --> 00:22:47,733
Oh, a monster appeared in your dream?
Is that what happened?

355
00:22:47,733 --> 00:22:51,833
Should I sing your favorite Baby Shark's
My Dream Is a Superhero?

356
00:22:51,833 --> 00:22:54,967
You know all the monsters run away
when we sing that song, right?

357
00:22:54,967 --> 00:22:56,200
Alright, good!

358
00:22:56,200 --> 00:22:58,267
Okay, I'm starting! Here we go.

359
00:22:58,267 --> 00:23:01,167
♪ I'm going to be a superhero ♪

360
00:23:01,167 --> 00:23:03,867
♪ I will save the whole wide world ♪

361
00:23:03,867 --> 00:23:06,000
♪ Bang, bang, bang ♪

362
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:08,992
♪ My dream is to be a superhero ♪

363
00:23:08,992 --> 00:23:10,792
How is it?

364
00:23:12,767 --> 00:23:15,867
- That gives me chills. It's creepy too.
- You like it?

365
00:23:15,867 --> 00:23:18,600
So, the great Kingfisher has become a mom?

366
00:23:18,600 --> 00:23:22,336
It's unfamiliar. It's very unfamiliar.

367
00:23:22,336 --> 00:23:25,100
♪ I'm going to be a superhero ♪

368
00:23:25,100 --> 00:23:27,867
♪ I will save the whole wide world ♪

369
00:23:27,867 --> 00:23:30,700
♪ Bang, bang, bang ♪

370
00:23:30,700 --> 00:23:34,300
♪ My dream is to be a superhero ♪

371
00:23:41,633 --> 00:23:44,800
Detective Lee Dong Jin, you're here.

372
00:23:44,800 --> 00:23:48,100
You must be working around the clock
with such a major case

373
00:23:48,100 --> 00:23:49,967
happening in your district.

374
00:23:49,967 --> 00:23:52,167
Please have a seat over here.

375
00:23:52,167 --> 00:23:55,133
Reporter Kwon Tae Seong, it's been a while.

376
00:23:55,133 --> 00:23:57,900
You only come looking for me
when something like this happens.

377
00:23:57,900 --> 00:23:59,600
Sorry.

378
00:24:00,600 --> 00:24:02,333
Hey, you're paying today.

379
00:24:02,333 --> 00:24:04,733
Come on, people are watching. Sit down.

380
00:24:04,733 --> 00:24:07,400
I already ordered. The most expensive one.

381
00:24:12,100 --> 00:24:13,700
Looks expensive.

382
00:24:14,333 --> 00:24:15,567
- Enjoy your meal.
- Yeah.

383
00:24:15,567 --> 00:24:17,233
Thank you.

384
00:24:19,767 --> 00:24:23,600
Just get to the point.
I have to head back right after I eat.

385
00:24:23,600 --> 00:24:26,733
You always act like you're busy.
I'm busy too.

386
00:24:27,600 --> 00:24:31,233
You're covering the Kingfisher story, right?
That's why you're here.

387
00:24:31,233 --> 00:24:34,733
The juniors handle that stuff now.
I've moved on.

388
00:24:34,733 --> 00:24:37,733
You saw the news.
It's exactly what it looks like.

389
00:24:37,733 --> 00:24:40,067
Nothing more to tell you.

390
00:24:43,567 --> 00:24:48,567
- No need to get you anything expensive.
- Hey, that's mine. Eat yours.

391
00:24:53,300 --> 00:24:55,100
Is it really the Kingfisher?

392
00:24:56,767 --> 00:25:01,233
Oh, my, why does everyone ask me that
the moment they see me?

393
00:25:02,367 --> 00:25:04,600
If I answer, will you write it?

394
00:25:04,600 --> 00:25:07,067
I told you I wouldn't.

395
00:25:07,767 --> 00:25:09,467
- You won't?
- I won't.

396
00:25:09,467 --> 00:25:11,067
Why not?

397
00:25:11,067 --> 00:25:13,200
You're the Kingfisher expert.

398
00:25:13,200 --> 00:25:15,900
Now that I think about it,
four years ago in Haegong-dong too...

399
00:25:15,900 --> 00:25:17,533
Is it Kingfisher?

400
00:25:28,533 --> 00:25:32,200
Well, the method
and victim profiles are similar,

401
00:25:32,200 --> 00:25:34,467
but it's still just speculation.

402
00:25:35,333 --> 00:25:37,733
The weapon is different,

403
00:25:37,733 --> 00:25:40,667
and the fact that he rarely carried out
daytime shootings bothers me.

404
00:25:40,667 --> 00:25:44,367
No, forget the official theory.
What's your gut telling you?

405
00:25:48,967 --> 00:25:52,400
One hundred percent Kingfisher.

406
00:25:56,333 --> 00:25:58,933
I thought he retired four years ago.

407
00:25:58,933 --> 00:26:02,100
Hey, what retirement does a killer have?

408
00:26:03,867 --> 00:26:08,267
What are the differences between
the case four years ago and this one?

409
00:26:08,267 --> 00:26:11,600
You were at both scenes, so you'd know.
Anything, even a small detail.

410
00:26:11,600 --> 00:26:14,167
Like, you found anything
at the shooting site...

411
00:26:15,233 --> 00:26:17,167
You're unbelievable.
Did you come here knowing something?

412
00:26:17,167 --> 00:26:19,400
You found something? What is it?

413
00:26:23,633 --> 00:26:25,133
Baby Shark.

414
00:26:25,133 --> 00:26:26,967
What?

415
00:26:26,967 --> 00:26:28,467
A sticker.

416
00:26:32,167 --> 00:26:34,200
What, a sticker?

417
00:26:34,200 --> 00:26:35,733
Yeah.

418
00:26:37,633 --> 00:26:42,000
I sent it to the NFS just in case,
but they said there were no fingerprints,

419
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:46,133
and that it was something you could
easily buy at most stores or online.

420
00:26:46,133 --> 00:26:49,567
Which means every household in Korea
with kids probably has one.

421
00:26:49,567 --> 00:26:51,900
Dozens of Baby Sharks.

422
00:26:51,900 --> 00:26:55,700
The sharks in our house even have babies.

423
00:26:58,500 --> 00:27:01,300
Looks like Kingfisher
is a Baby Shark fanatic just like my Yul.

424
00:27:01,300 --> 00:27:04,633
Hey, this would blow up the views
if I wrote about it.

425
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:13,867
This is good.

426
00:27:13,867 --> 00:27:16,433
Yul, what did you play with Chae Won today?

427
00:27:16,433 --> 00:27:18,767
[Baby Shark]
We played with this sticker.

428
00:27:18,767 --> 00:27:20,133
It's a Baby Shark sticker!

429
00:27:20,133 --> 00:27:21,933
Should I stick one on you too? This one?

430
00:27:21,933 --> 00:27:23,800
Should I put one on? Where should I put it?

431
00:27:23,800 --> 00:27:27,267
Mommy is the mommy shark.

432
00:27:27,267 --> 00:27:29,467
Mommy shark?

433
00:27:29,467 --> 00:27:32,333
This makes my clothes look even prettier.

434
00:27:32,333 --> 00:27:34,767
So what did you put on today?

435
00:27:34,767 --> 00:27:36,700
- Baby Shark.
- You put on a Baby Shark?

436
00:27:36,700 --> 00:27:39,700
This one is cute too. It looks like you.

437
00:27:39,700 --> 00:27:40,767
Yul!

438
00:27:40,767 --> 00:27:42,933
Daddy!

439
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:46,133
My little precious!

440
00:27:46,133 --> 00:27:48,267
Come here, my big precious.

441
00:27:52,400 --> 00:27:55,667
Honey, why are you home so early?
Aren't you busy?

442
00:27:55,667 --> 00:27:58,200
I am busy. But today,
in the middle of all that,

443
00:27:58,200 --> 00:28:01,800
I had a sudden realization
that I missed my wife so much!

444
00:28:01,800 --> 00:28:03,567
What could I do then?
I had to run right over.

445
00:28:03,567 --> 00:28:08,100
Really? Why did you miss me so much today?

446
00:28:10,367 --> 00:28:11,567
You did something wrong, right?

447
00:28:11,567 --> 00:28:14,833
What would I have done wrong?
It's not like that, really.

448
00:28:14,833 --> 00:28:18,000
I really just wanted to see you,
so I came. Seriously.

449
00:28:18,000 --> 00:28:22,533
Then we must be connected by telepathy.
I really missed you today too.

450
00:28:22,533 --> 00:28:23,600
Really?

451
00:28:23,600 --> 00:28:25,100
Yeah.

452
00:28:33,200 --> 00:28:37,133
What is it?
Something happened today, didn't it?

453
00:28:37,133 --> 00:28:40,767
What do you mean? I'm just tired
from the business trip yesterday.

454
00:28:40,767 --> 00:28:42,833
Since we're already out,
should we grab dinner before going home?

455
00:28:42,833 --> 00:28:44,767
Yeah! Chicken! Chicken!

456
00:28:44,767 --> 00:28:47,167
Yul, do you want chicken?

457
00:28:47,167 --> 00:28:48,733
Should we go to Grandma's and eat chicken?

458
00:28:48,733 --> 00:28:51,400
Grandma's chicken is the best!

459
00:28:51,400 --> 00:28:52,933
Let's go.

460
00:28:52,933 --> 00:28:55,833
Let's go eat chicken.

461
00:29:03,267 --> 00:29:04,333
Enjoy your meal!

462
00:29:04,333 --> 00:29:06,433
- Let me know if you need anything.
- Grandma, Auntie!

463
00:29:06,433 --> 00:29:08,533
Pretty Yul is here.

464
00:29:08,533 --> 00:29:10,067
What brings you here at this hour?

465
00:29:10,067 --> 00:29:12,192
Oh, my, our pretty Yul is here?

466
00:29:12,192 --> 00:29:14,333
My son is here!

467
00:29:14,333 --> 00:29:16,400
Hey, come out here for a sec.

468
00:29:16,400 --> 00:29:18,900
Why is it so hard to see you these days?

469
00:29:18,900 --> 00:29:22,233
Oh, my, my little Yul!

470
00:29:24,733 --> 00:29:27,400
Yul, say hello to Grandma.
Give her a big greeting.

471
00:29:27,400 --> 00:29:29,233
Hello, Grandma.

472
00:29:29,233 --> 00:29:31,467
Good girl!

473
00:29:31,467 --> 00:29:34,867
But what brings you here?
Did you come straight from work?

474
00:29:34,867 --> 00:29:38,000
We ran into each other near home,
and Yul said she wanted chicken.

475
00:29:38,000 --> 00:29:40,067
Oh, did you?

476
00:29:40,067 --> 00:29:42,400
- Then come sit down. Sit down.
- Sit down.

477
00:29:43,033 --> 00:29:46,767
I will fry up
the most delicious chicken for my Yul!

478
00:29:46,767 --> 00:29:48,300
Okay.

479
00:29:49,833 --> 00:29:52,567
Since you're here anyway, stay and eat.

480
00:29:52,567 --> 00:29:56,133
But it's not good for children or adults
to eat takeout food too often.

481
00:29:56,133 --> 00:30:00,400
People who work outside all day
should come home to a warm homemade meal.

482
00:30:00,400 --> 00:30:02,400
It was me who wanted it.

483
00:30:02,400 --> 00:30:04,533
Okay, Mother.

484
00:30:06,433 --> 00:30:07,933
I was the one who asked...

485
00:30:09,067 --> 00:30:10,100
Welcome!

486
00:30:10,100 --> 00:30:13,400
- Sun Il, I should've done that. Sorry.
- Oh, please, sit down.

487
00:30:13,400 --> 00:30:15,800
Hey, hold it in today.

488
00:30:15,800 --> 00:30:18,300
Mom's finally in a good mood
after a while. Don't ruin it.

489
00:30:18,300 --> 00:30:21,733
Why? Why is Mom in a good mood?

490
00:30:21,733 --> 00:30:25,133
The landlord said
they'd freeze the rent again.

491
00:30:25,133 --> 00:30:29,467
Other shops raise their rent every year,
but ours hasn't changed for years.

492
00:30:29,467 --> 00:30:32,233
She was bragging about it to everyone.

493
00:30:32,233 --> 00:30:35,267
That's really kind of the landlord.
It's not easy to do that these days.

494
00:30:35,267 --> 00:30:37,300
Such an angel.

495
00:30:37,300 --> 00:30:39,300
We're busy right now, so wait just a little.

496
00:30:39,300 --> 00:30:40,767
Wait just a moment, Yul.

497
00:30:40,767 --> 00:30:42,300
Okay.

498
00:30:43,200 --> 00:30:45,867
I'm back!

499
00:30:45,867 --> 00:30:47,733
Bo Na, you're here?

500
00:30:47,733 --> 00:30:48,800
Auntie!

501
00:30:48,800 --> 00:30:52,233
Oh, my! Our cute Yul is here?

502
00:30:52,233 --> 00:30:54,100
Did you just finish a delivery?

503
00:30:54,100 --> 00:30:56,160
Yeah. Is it some special day?

504
00:30:56,160 --> 00:30:59,000
We got a bunch of
delivery orders all at once.

505
00:30:59,000 --> 00:31:00,333
You said you'd drink water, so drink up.

506
00:31:00,333 --> 00:31:03,467
By the way, why are you here
at this hour? Aren't you busy?

507
00:31:03,467 --> 00:31:04,867
I heard Kingfisher showed up.

508
00:31:04,867 --> 00:31:06,784
That was ages ago.
That's not my thing anymore.

509
00:31:06,784 --> 00:31:09,333
What about you? So, how have you been?

510
00:31:09,333 --> 00:31:11,567
Seriously, what have you been
hearing all this time?

511
00:31:11,567 --> 00:31:13,233
Same old, same old.

512
00:31:13,233 --> 00:31:17,200
I mean, I do have a social position
as a graduate student.

513
00:31:17,200 --> 00:31:20,767
But to Mom, that's the same
as being an unemployed bum.

514
00:31:20,767 --> 00:31:22,200
- Ah, seriously...
- That's why

515
00:31:22,200 --> 00:31:23,967
I keep telling you to hire part-timers.

516
00:31:23,967 --> 00:31:26,752
How can we afford
to hire people and pay them?

517
00:31:26,752 --> 00:31:28,533
Family members have to work hard together.

518
00:31:28,533 --> 00:31:33,133
You exploit your daughter for cheap labor.
You're a terrible employer!

519
00:31:33,133 --> 00:31:34,933
A terrible employer.

520
00:31:34,933 --> 00:31:36,733
All you do is talk.

521
00:31:36,733 --> 00:31:38,267
You know your sister-in-law
went back to work, right?

522
00:31:38,267 --> 00:31:41,033
- Yeah.
- If you look after Yul sometimes,

523
00:31:41,033 --> 00:31:46,200
I might, you know, increase your allowance.

524
00:31:46,200 --> 00:31:47,667
Really?

525
00:31:47,667 --> 00:31:52,533
Of course, I'd do anything for our Yul
even without allowance!

526
00:31:52,533 --> 00:31:56,000
But if you offer, I'll gladly accept.

527
00:31:56,900 --> 00:32:00,267
- I'll chip in too. Please help us.
- Done!

528
00:32:00,267 --> 00:32:02,700
Bo Na, how is it being back
at work? Do you like it?

529
00:32:02,700 --> 00:32:05,367
Oh, there's no way it could be good.
Is the work manageable?

530
00:32:05,367 --> 00:32:06,633
[Tae Seong Chicken]
Oh, dear.

531
00:32:06,633 --> 00:32:08,767
Why are you sitting in the customer's seat?
Hurry and go deliver.

532
00:32:08,767 --> 00:32:10,800
How is he a customer?

533
00:32:10,800 --> 00:32:12,333
The deliveries are piling up.

534
00:32:12,333 --> 00:32:13,933
Then at least pay me more.

535
00:32:13,933 --> 00:32:15,467
I'll be back.

536
00:32:19,733 --> 00:32:22,700
Did he go to prison for another crime?

537
00:32:22,700 --> 00:32:25,200
Was he seriously injured or sick?

538
00:32:25,920 --> 00:32:29,633
A vacation... A leave of absence?

539
00:32:29,633 --> 00:32:31,233
You've been saying that since earlier.

540
00:32:31,233 --> 00:32:35,500
What? Is being a murderer a job?
Retirement, leave of absence, vacation?

541
00:32:39,667 --> 00:32:44,533
He could've gotten married,
started a family, and had kids, like me.

542
00:32:44,533 --> 00:32:47,033
Even Kingfisher
could get married, unlike you...

543
00:32:47,733 --> 00:32:49,733
Watch what you say.
There's a gun at the station.

544
00:32:49,733 --> 00:32:51,367
Hey, that's disgusting! Hey!

545
00:32:51,367 --> 00:32:53,184
That's why you should get married, idiot.

546
00:32:53,184 --> 00:32:55,667
Stop living alone like some pathetic loser.

547
00:32:57,280 --> 00:33:01,300
Fine, let's say
your ridiculous theory is true.

548
00:33:01,300 --> 00:33:04,768
If he got married, built a family,
and had a kid, why come back?

549
00:33:04,768 --> 00:33:06,467
Why not just keep living that life?

550
00:33:06,467 --> 00:33:07,900
Because he couldn't stand not killing people?

551
00:33:07,900 --> 00:33:11,100
Or what, because he's some hero
who wants attention?

552
00:33:11,100 --> 00:33:14,333
Or maybe because life got boring?

553
00:33:15,133 --> 00:33:18,333
Why are you asking me?
Ask him yourself when you catch him.

554
00:33:18,333 --> 00:33:21,536
And ask him if he's really
a Baby Shark fanatic too.

555
00:33:21,536 --> 00:33:23,104
- Hey, you.
- Hey, who knows?

556
00:33:23,104 --> 00:33:26,500
That sticker might really have been a clue.

557
00:33:26,500 --> 00:33:28,700
You never know.

558
00:33:42,333 --> 00:33:43,567
Daddy, it's good.

559
00:33:43,567 --> 00:33:45,167
Is it good?

560
00:33:45,167 --> 00:33:47,233
I think it's delicious too.

561
00:33:49,367 --> 00:33:54,100
Yul, you can do this, right?

562
00:33:56,672 --> 00:33:58,233
I'll give it to you.

563
00:34:01,184 --> 00:34:02,600
Is it good?

564
00:34:02,600 --> 00:34:04,500
Yul, you learned how to do this, right?

565
00:34:04,500 --> 00:34:07,100
You're a big girl now,
so you can do it, right?

566
00:34:21,300 --> 00:34:23,392
[Yoo Bo Na's Relationship Chart]

567
00:34:33,400 --> 00:34:35,904
[Durumi Electronics Sales Team 3,
Killer Group]

568
00:36:06,433 --> 00:36:09,733
You're already awake? It's still early.

569
00:36:09,733 --> 00:36:11,467
I had a bad dream.

570
00:36:11,467 --> 00:36:16,367
I woke up and got scared
because you weren't there.

571
00:36:16,367 --> 00:36:18,600
A bad dream? What kind of dream?

572
00:36:18,600 --> 00:36:20,400
A dream where someone took you away.

573
00:36:20,400 --> 00:36:23,700
Who? Who took me?

574
00:36:23,700 --> 00:36:24,767
A monster.

575
00:36:24,767 --> 00:36:26,233
What? What is that?

576
00:36:26,233 --> 00:36:29,733
It's real. In my dream,
a really scary monster took you away.

577
00:36:29,733 --> 00:36:31,867
You're in big trouble now.

578
00:36:33,433 --> 00:36:38,367
No, maybe I'm the one who's in trouble.
I can't live without you.

579
00:36:38,367 --> 00:36:41,600
Then I guess I should sing
Baby Shark's Superhero for you.

580
00:36:41,600 --> 00:36:43,433
Apparently, it's the perfect weapon
against monsters.

581
00:36:43,433 --> 00:36:45,067
- Really?
- Yeah.

582
00:36:45,067 --> 00:36:46,467
Sing it.

583
00:36:46,467 --> 00:36:47,500
Sing it for me.

584
00:36:47,500 --> 00:36:51,867
Go back inside and get some more sleep.
I'll take Yul to daycare today.

585
00:36:59,767 --> 00:37:03,167
Let's just stay like this for one minute.

586
00:37:14,767 --> 00:37:18,200
[Durumi Electronics]

587
00:37:42,300 --> 00:37:44,267
Good morning!

588
00:39:03,167 --> 00:39:04,933
[Security Alert]

589
00:39:07,900 --> 00:39:11,633
Hey, when did Tae Min leave
without saying anything?

590
00:39:13,267 --> 00:39:15,767
[Unregistered Entrant Detected]
What, he brought someone with him?

591
00:39:17,833 --> 00:39:21,433
She's finally here! Our team's newbie!

592
00:39:22,367 --> 00:39:24,267
Wow!

593
00:39:26,000 --> 00:39:27,600
[Bong Tae Min]

594
00:39:31,192 --> 00:39:32,192
[Not Today]

595
00:39:32,192 --> 00:39:34,267
What? The case has been...

596
00:39:36,167 --> 00:39:38,133
The case has been closed?

597
00:39:40,233 --> 00:39:41,733
Just a moment.

598
00:39:43,433 --> 00:39:44,967
The investigation is already over?

599
00:39:44,967 --> 00:39:46,700
What about the NFS results?
Did they come out?

600
00:39:46,700 --> 00:39:50,067
They did come out,
but there was nothing significant.

601
00:39:50,067 --> 00:39:51,100
[Bae Doo Hyuk Car Explosion Case]

602
00:39:51,100 --> 00:39:54,867
It has been classified
as an accidental death.

603
00:39:54,867 --> 00:39:56,467
An accidental death?

604
00:39:56,467 --> 00:39:58,767
So you're saying it wasn't murder,
but an accident?

605
00:39:58,767 --> 00:40:03,367
Wow, our new employee
brought this on her first day.

606
00:40:03,367 --> 00:40:05,367
She's got great taste, right?

607
00:40:05,367 --> 00:40:06,467
Yeah.

608
00:40:06,467 --> 00:40:09,500
Then we should do proper introductions.

609
00:40:09,500 --> 00:40:11,967
As I've mentioned before,

610
00:40:11,967 --> 00:40:15,867
this is our new team member
who will be working with us, Ms. Oh Hyun Nam.

611
00:40:17,233 --> 00:40:20,367
Nice to meet you.
I look forward to working with you.

612
00:40:20,367 --> 00:40:22,000
Welcome!

613
00:40:24,933 --> 00:40:26,800
Same here. It's nice to meet you.

614
00:40:26,800 --> 00:40:30,784
Oh, Ms. Hyun Nam has been working alone
as a freelancer until now,

615
00:40:30,784 --> 00:40:33,248
so this is her first time working
in a team and company environment.

616
00:40:33,248 --> 00:40:35,300
Please help her out.

617
00:40:35,300 --> 00:40:37,833
Let me properly introduce everyone
on our team.

618
00:40:37,833 --> 00:40:40,700
This is Assistant Manager Yang Ye Sol.

619
00:40:40,700 --> 00:40:44,367
Her job is forging all kinds of documents.

620
00:40:44,367 --> 00:40:46,600
- How well?
- Perfectly.

621
00:40:46,600 --> 00:40:48,064
[Business Trip Application]
Please come to me

622
00:40:48,064 --> 00:40:49,233
for anything related to paperwork.

623
00:40:49,233 --> 00:40:52,567
[Destination: Musan, Reason: Client Meeting]

624
00:40:53,633 --> 00:40:55,200
Alright.

625
00:40:55,200 --> 00:40:56,533
You startled me.

626
00:40:56,533 --> 00:41:01,233
Were you there the whole time?
That's Manager Bong Tae Min.

627
00:41:01,233 --> 00:41:02,688
We don't call him Manager Bong, though.

628
00:41:02,688 --> 00:41:05,367
We call him Manager Tae or Manager Tae Min.

629
00:41:05,367 --> 00:41:09,333
He handles the cutting-edge equipment there.

630
00:41:10,767 --> 00:41:13,167
Well, that guy...

631
00:41:13,167 --> 00:41:15,167
Is he kept isolated separately?

632
00:41:15,167 --> 00:41:18,333
Isolated? Well, yeah.
It's more of self-isolation.

633
00:41:18,333 --> 00:41:21,367
None of us likes going into that room.

634
00:41:21,367 --> 00:41:23,200
You'll understand later.

635
00:41:26,767 --> 00:41:31,033
It's simple. No need for a long explanation.

636
00:41:31,033 --> 00:41:33,433
A portable LPG gas canister,
burned completely black,

637
00:41:33,433 --> 00:41:36,576
was found in the trunk of Bae Doo Hyuk's car.

638
00:41:36,576 --> 00:41:39,936
It turns out the valve was slightly open.

639
00:41:39,936 --> 00:41:41,733
This is...

640
00:41:41,733 --> 00:41:45,267
better known as Dr. Go.

641
00:41:45,267 --> 00:41:50,267
His job is making any death
look like a medical accident.

642
00:41:50,267 --> 00:41:51,367
How well?

643
00:41:51,367 --> 00:41:53,333
Perfectly.

644
00:41:53,333 --> 00:41:55,367
I'm a real doctor.

645
00:42:02,767 --> 00:42:05,200
The driver is going to the restroom.

646
00:42:05,200 --> 00:42:06,233
Assistant Manager Ki Yeong Do.

647
00:42:06,233 --> 00:42:10,267
Oh, he can do anything with computers.
He's our team's genius hacker.

648
00:42:11,200 --> 00:42:13,133
Nice to meet you.

649
00:42:13,133 --> 00:42:14,633
Yeah.

650
00:42:15,867 --> 00:42:19,367
Oh, I forgot to introduce myself.

651
00:42:19,367 --> 00:42:23,008
I'm Kim Bong Pal,

652
00:42:23,008 --> 00:42:26,833
the leader of Sales Team 3.

653
00:42:26,833 --> 00:42:31,367
My last name is actually Kim,
but everyone just calls me Team Leader Bong.

654
00:42:34,533 --> 00:42:36,233
What I do is...

655
00:42:41,500 --> 00:42:44,167
You're saying there are
absolutely no signs of foul play?

656
00:42:44,167 --> 00:42:47,867
If someone put the gas tank in there
or deliberately opened the valve...

657
00:42:47,867 --> 00:42:51,033
Then there should've been footage of it.

658
00:42:51,033 --> 00:42:53,900
But we checked all the CCTV outside the club

659
00:42:53,900 --> 00:42:56,667
and all the dashcam footage
from the parking lot, and there's nothing.

660
00:42:56,667 --> 00:42:59,333
It was pure luck. A miracle.

661
00:42:59,333 --> 00:43:02,800
Well, there's usually a separate driver.

662
00:43:02,800 --> 00:43:05,333
But that day the driver
had a sudden stomach problem.

663
00:43:05,333 --> 00:43:08,833
Well, as for the gas tank,
Bae Doo Hyuk must've put it there himself.

664
00:43:08,833 --> 00:43:11,100
You know where Bae Doo Hyuk was going?

665
00:43:11,100 --> 00:43:13,467
His girlfriend was waiting
for him at a nearby villa.

666
00:43:13,467 --> 00:43:16,467
Maybe they were planning to have
a barbecue together or something.

667
00:43:16,467 --> 00:43:19,233
At least it happened
in a quiet suburban area.

668
00:43:19,233 --> 00:43:21,267
If it had happened downtown...

669
00:43:21,267 --> 00:43:23,100
Oh, dear.

670
00:43:23,100 --> 00:43:25,900
Quiet location. Good.

671
00:43:25,900 --> 00:43:30,567
Once the taxi is more than
100 meters away, we'll go.

672
00:43:32,467 --> 00:43:35,700
Now, client meeting starts.

673
00:43:47,633 --> 00:43:49,433
Meeting clear.

674
00:43:50,967 --> 00:43:55,000
Rest in peace. I can't tell you to be reborn.

675
00:43:55,000 --> 00:43:58,867
Whether they die or survive,
I make it all look like an accident.

676
00:43:58,867 --> 00:44:00,900
How well? Perfectly.

677
00:44:00,900 --> 00:44:05,800
Simply put, you could say
he died an unfortunate death.

678
00:44:05,800 --> 00:44:07,633
What a fate...

679
00:44:08,300 --> 00:44:10,267
Isn't something a little strange?

680
00:44:10,267 --> 00:44:13,933
Everything lines up perfectly.
Like someone planned the whole thing.

681
00:44:13,933 --> 00:44:16,633
Bae Doo Hyuk wasn't just involved in drugs.

682
00:44:16,633 --> 00:44:21,000
He was known for framing his underlings
for murders he ordered.

683
00:44:21,000 --> 00:44:22,667
It's a known fact in that world.

684
00:44:22,667 --> 00:44:26,133
Who knows how many
other crimes he got away with?

685
00:44:26,133 --> 00:44:28,100
Exactly my point.
Which is why it is even more...

686
00:44:28,100 --> 00:44:29,267
He was such a piece of work.

687
00:44:29,267 --> 00:44:33,433
Honestly, a guy like him getting gunned down
by the Kingfisher is just unsurprising.

688
00:44:33,433 --> 00:44:35,600
Well, detectives speak with evidence,

689
00:44:35,600 --> 00:44:37,867
and you, the reporter,
should write with facts.

690
00:44:37,867 --> 00:44:41,567
With everyone already worked up
over Kingfisher, who would even care?

691
00:44:41,567 --> 00:44:45,033
Anyway, we've closed the case,
so just know that.

692
00:44:45,033 --> 00:44:47,328
And don't call me again.

693
00:44:47,328 --> 00:44:48,533
Hello...

694
00:44:48,533 --> 00:44:51,100
But public sentiment is different.

695
00:44:51,100 --> 00:44:54,367
Because he only targets the worst criminals,

696
00:44:54,367 --> 00:44:58,033
some people are becoming
obsessed with Kingfisher.

697
00:44:58,033 --> 00:45:00,833
The Kingfisher fan club
already has over a million members.

698
00:45:00,833 --> 00:45:02,267
He targets the worst of the worst,

699
00:45:02,267 --> 00:45:06,033
especially those
who escaped proper punishment,

700
00:45:06,033 --> 00:45:08,767
so isn't it natural that people frustrated
with the flawed justice system

701
00:45:08,767 --> 00:45:10,567
are drawn to him?

702
00:45:10,567 --> 00:45:14,967
A powerful hero who punishes evil
in place of a powerless law.

703
00:45:14,967 --> 00:45:18,033
Lastly, our ace.

704
00:45:18,033 --> 00:45:22,233
The face of Sales Team 3, Director Yoo Bo Na.

705
00:45:24,267 --> 00:45:25,700
As for Director Yoo...

706
00:45:25,700 --> 00:45:28,433
I know who she is.

707
00:45:38,800 --> 00:45:42,467
It's an honor to meet you, Kingfisher.

708
00:45:49,000 --> 00:45:52,633
The pleasure's mine, Ms. Oh Hyun Nam.

709
00:45:55,400 --> 00:45:58,900
Let's work well together from now on.

710
00:45:58,900 --> 00:46:00,400
"Together"?

711
00:46:04,367 --> 00:46:06,500
Yeah, let's work well together.

712
00:46:13,700 --> 00:46:14,800
Where's my desk?

713
00:46:14,800 --> 00:46:17,967
Oh, right here. Next to Assistant Manager Ki.

714
00:46:19,033 --> 00:46:22,433
All right, everyone. Back to work.

715
00:46:24,767 --> 00:46:26,467
Oh, right.

716
00:46:26,467 --> 00:46:28,700
I forgot to tell you what I do.

717
00:46:28,700 --> 00:46:30,300
Oh, you're right.

718
00:46:31,033 --> 00:46:32,700
I handle poisonings.

719
00:46:32,700 --> 00:46:36,288
Slip poison into food or drinks,
and no one ever knows perfectly.

720
00:46:40,133 --> 00:46:43,867
So, how about pork belly with water dropwort
for tonight's team dinner?

721
00:46:43,867 --> 00:46:44,967
Water dropwort is great for detoxing.

722
00:46:44,967 --> 00:46:46,167
Then make the arrangements.

723
00:46:46,167 --> 00:46:49,200
- Yeah, I'll book the place.
- Good.

724
00:47:01,600 --> 00:47:04,933
I've finished the article, so it's fine.

725
00:47:04,933 --> 00:47:10,133
I'll take care of Yul,
so don't worry and enjoy yourself.

726
00:47:10,133 --> 00:47:15,900
It's your welcome-back dinner too.
The guest of honor can't miss it.

727
00:47:15,900 --> 00:47:18,167
Then I'm counting on you tonight.

728
00:47:18,167 --> 00:47:20,867
When you get home,
wash Yul's hands and feet first, okay?

729
00:47:20,867 --> 00:47:24,167
And there's curry
and beef radish soup in the fridge...

730
00:47:24,167 --> 00:47:26,700
I can handle it.

731
00:47:27,900 --> 00:47:32,333
Okay, lecture over! I'll call you
when we're wrapping up.

732
00:47:32,333 --> 00:47:33,833
See you later.

733
00:47:39,680 --> 00:47:42,080
[Musan Drug Kingpin's
Car Explosion Ruled an Accident]

734
00:47:51,168 --> 00:47:52,168
[Musan Drug Kingpin's
Car Explosion Ruled an Accident]

735
00:47:54,967 --> 00:47:56,600
That's over, I see.

736
00:47:59,467 --> 00:48:00,800
Yeah, well, for now.

737
00:48:00,800 --> 00:48:03,867
"For now"? Does that mean
there's a second step?

738
00:48:03,867 --> 00:48:06,800
Forget it. From now on,
you're going after Kingfisher, right?

739
00:48:06,800 --> 00:48:08,867
"What did he do for 4 years,
and why did he come back without dying?"

740
00:48:08,867 --> 00:48:09,933
Well, something more in-depth.

741
00:48:09,933 --> 00:48:11,033
I'll get going.

742
00:48:11,033 --> 00:48:13,167
Oh, leaving already?

743
00:48:13,167 --> 00:48:16,267
Where to first? The NFS?
The crime scene? The police station?

744
00:48:16,267 --> 00:48:18,267
No. I'm picking up my daughter.

745
00:48:18,267 --> 00:48:20,433
- Your daughter?
- My wife is running late today.

746
00:48:20,433 --> 00:48:21,967
Oh, boy.

747
00:48:21,967 --> 00:48:23,767
I'll get going then.

748
00:48:23,767 --> 00:48:26,333
Hey, Tae Seong, you punk!

749
00:48:27,433 --> 00:48:28,960
Well, what's gotten into him?

750
00:48:28,960 --> 00:48:31,584
One bottle of soju, please!

751
00:48:33,067 --> 00:48:34,233
Dig in, everyone.

752
00:48:34,233 --> 00:48:36,033
Yeah.

753
00:48:36,033 --> 00:48:41,267
Director Yoo, don't you ever
get to eat meat at home or...

754
00:48:43,200 --> 00:48:48,467
We're more of a chicken family.
This pork is really amazing.

755
00:48:48,467 --> 00:48:51,900
The best part about coming back to work
is definitely the company dinners.

756
00:48:51,900 --> 00:48:55,480
Absolutely. Team dinners
are the best part of office life.

757
00:48:55,480 --> 00:48:56,480
That's true.

758
00:48:56,480 --> 00:48:58,000
- Alright.
- Cheers!

759
00:48:58,000 --> 00:49:00,033
Sales Team 3, fighting!

760
00:49:00,033 --> 00:49:03,008
- Fighting!
- Cheers!

761
00:49:08,300 --> 00:49:09,833
This is so good.

762
00:49:09,833 --> 00:49:10,867
Good, huh?

763
00:49:10,867 --> 00:49:12,667
Want a drink, Ms. Yoo?

764
00:49:15,067 --> 00:49:17,033
Oh, no!

765
00:49:17,033 --> 00:49:19,600
- Don't.
- I'll just smell it.

766
00:49:21,633 --> 00:49:24,533
Director Yoo hasn't touched alcohol
since she got married.

767
00:49:24,533 --> 00:49:30,700
Honestly, that's for the best.
She gets pretty wild when she drinks.

768
00:49:32,267 --> 00:49:35,133
By the way, I was really surprised.

769
00:49:35,133 --> 00:49:37,900
I heard that Hyun Nam
is the developer of that famous 'Mist'?

770
00:49:37,900 --> 00:49:39,900
Exactly.

771
00:49:39,900 --> 00:49:43,000
Now that Director Yoo is back

772
00:49:43,000 --> 00:49:44,467
and someone as talented
as Hyun Nam has joined us,

773
00:49:44,467 --> 00:49:48,933
Sales Team 3 is basically
the Avengers now, right?

774
00:49:48,933 --> 00:49:50,267
Absolutely.

775
00:49:50,267 --> 00:49:53,033
By the way, what exactly is 'Mist'?

776
00:49:53,033 --> 00:49:56,400
I guess you don't know about it,
Assistant Manager Yang.

777
00:49:59,833 --> 00:50:01,800
Gather around.

778
00:50:03,808 --> 00:50:10,667
Mist is the name of the poison
that's claimed the most lives

779
00:50:10,667 --> 00:50:12,733
in recent years.

780
00:50:12,733 --> 00:50:15,133
It's about 10,000 times
more toxic than arsenic

781
00:50:15,133 --> 00:50:18,567
and roughly 100 times
more potent than tetrodotoxin.

782
00:50:18,567 --> 00:50:23,533
No autopsy will ever detect a trace of it.

783
00:50:23,533 --> 00:50:28,533
By then, it naturally breaks down
and leaves almost no trace in the body.

784
00:50:28,533 --> 00:50:31,567
What do you think? Perfectly, right?

785
00:50:32,900 --> 00:50:37,433
For our line of work,
it's the perfect poison.

786
00:50:38,233 --> 00:50:40,400
That's incredible!

787
00:50:40,400 --> 00:50:43,033
How did you create something like that?

788
00:50:43,033 --> 00:50:45,433
Well, it just happened.

789
00:50:45,433 --> 00:50:47,300
"Well, it just happened."

790
00:50:48,833 --> 00:50:50,200
But I'm curious.

791
00:50:50,200 --> 00:50:53,133
With skills like yours,
you could've stayed independent.

792
00:50:53,800 --> 00:50:56,667
Why join this team?

793
00:50:58,800 --> 00:50:59,800
Hold on.

794
00:50:59,800 --> 00:51:01,333
Oh, Director Yoo!

795
00:51:03,933 --> 00:51:06,367
I have a debt to repay.

796
00:51:10,167 --> 00:51:11,200
What did you do today, Yul?

797
00:51:11,200 --> 00:51:13,000
Ta-da!

798
00:51:13,000 --> 00:51:15,033
I drew Mommy and Daddy, and Yul.

799
00:51:15,033 --> 00:51:17,267
Wow, that's a great drawing, Yul!

800
00:51:17,267 --> 00:51:19,633
But why did you draw Daddy better?

801
00:51:19,633 --> 00:51:25,233
Because Yul loves Daddy more, right?

802
00:51:25,233 --> 00:51:29,376
No, Yul loves Mommy more, right?
You love Mommy more, don't you?

803
00:51:29,376 --> 00:51:35,392
No. I love both Mommy and Daddy.

804
00:51:36,367 --> 00:51:41,400
I love Yul too. Love you! Heart!

805
00:51:41,400 --> 00:51:42,867
I'll be home soon.

806
00:51:42,867 --> 00:51:45,800
See you later, Mommy!

807
00:51:47,100 --> 00:51:48,300
So cute.

808
00:51:48,300 --> 00:51:50,967
It's a shame no one else
gets to see it, Kingfisher.

809
00:51:50,967 --> 00:51:53,600
You're having all the fun by yourself.

810
00:52:02,133 --> 00:52:05,200
Don't worry. No one would believe it anyway.

811
00:52:05,200 --> 00:52:09,967
Who'd ever imagine
the infamous Kingfisher is a married mom?

812
00:52:23,567 --> 00:52:26,733
Hyun Nam, do you have Mist?

813
00:52:28,800 --> 00:52:34,833
No, not the drinkable kind, the spray kind.
My clothes smell like pork barbecue.

814
00:52:34,833 --> 00:52:36,384
Got any?

815
00:52:36,384 --> 00:52:37,984
Oh, gosh.

816
00:52:44,867 --> 00:52:47,467
A lot of people would be disappointed.

817
00:52:47,467 --> 00:52:49,600
You're practically worshiped as a hero.

818
00:52:49,600 --> 00:52:52,533
If they found out you're living
such an ordinary family life...

819
00:52:52,533 --> 00:52:54,433
You think so?

820
00:52:54,433 --> 00:52:59,100
Have you ever wished you could
go back to your old life?

821
00:53:01,133 --> 00:53:03,867
Even married women say
they think that sometimes.

822
00:53:03,867 --> 00:53:08,800
Like wanting to go back to the carefree,
glamorous days of being single.

823
00:53:09,433 --> 00:53:13,300
Not at all. I like my life now.

824
00:53:14,533 --> 00:53:18,133
Because everything
that matters to me is right here.

825
00:53:19,233 --> 00:53:21,433
I see.

826
00:53:21,433 --> 00:53:23,000
Then why did you come back?

827
00:53:23,000 --> 00:53:25,500
You could've just kept living
that happy little life.

828
00:53:25,500 --> 00:53:27,933
Then why did you join this team, Hyun Nam?

829
00:53:27,933 --> 00:53:30,367
Did you come here to see me?

830
00:53:30,367 --> 00:53:34,067
Well, it just seemed like
you've been watching me all night.

831
00:53:34,067 --> 00:53:38,333
I wondered if you were my fan.
Or maybe an anti-fan?

832
00:53:38,333 --> 00:53:42,533
They say former fans
make the scariest haters.

833
00:53:42,533 --> 00:53:45,800
That's a little childish.

834
00:53:51,867 --> 00:53:56,333
Oh Hyun Nam, everyone makes choices.

835
00:53:56,333 --> 00:53:59,767
Those choices shape a person's life.

836
00:53:59,767 --> 00:54:02,624
Everyone makes
what they believe is the best choice

837
00:54:02,624 --> 00:54:04,933
because their life matters to them.

838
00:54:04,933 --> 00:54:08,800
And I think those choices deserve respect.

839
00:54:08,800 --> 00:54:10,567
I'm not here to listen to lectures...

840
00:54:10,567 --> 00:54:16,733
Just like it was your own choice
to do this work and join this company.

841
00:54:16,733 --> 00:54:21,000
No one forced you in
or pushed you out, right?

842
00:54:26,100 --> 00:54:30,333
If you're looking to play hero,
you've come to the wrong place.

843
00:54:30,333 --> 00:54:33,433
That's for Baby Sharks.

844
00:54:33,433 --> 00:54:35,167
Not us.

845
00:54:37,267 --> 00:54:39,033
What if...

846
00:54:40,000 --> 00:54:43,967
What would you do if you lost
the things that matter most to you?

847
00:54:46,067 --> 00:54:47,567
I don't know.

848
00:54:48,500 --> 00:54:50,533
I've never thought about it.

849
00:54:51,200 --> 00:54:53,133
Because I don't believe
that will ever happen.

850
00:55:09,133 --> 00:55:11,667
[Caller ID Restricted:
I'd like to provide a tip about Kingfisher]

851
00:55:38,867 --> 00:55:40,200
May I take your order?

852
00:55:40,200 --> 00:55:43,167
One iced Americano, please.

853
00:55:48,267 --> 00:55:51,667
Are you going to be late today?
I'm finishing early today.

854
00:55:52,533 --> 00:55:54,000
Really?

855
00:55:54,000 --> 00:55:56,933
I just have one meeting with an informant,
and then I'll be done too.

856
00:55:57,967 --> 00:56:00,600
Then how about we go on a date for a change?

857
00:56:00,600 --> 00:56:04,033
Se Ah said she'll watch Yul.
Guess she could use a little spending money.

858
00:56:05,900 --> 00:56:10,033
Of course, it's okay with me.
As expected, the power of pocket money!

859
00:56:13,767 --> 00:56:15,367
Thanks!

860
00:56:32,400 --> 00:56:33,633
Alright!

861
00:56:33,633 --> 00:56:38,467
Today is your last chance to take it easy,
so head home early.

862
00:56:38,467 --> 00:56:42,733
And you all know vacation days
are off the table for a while, right?

863
00:56:42,733 --> 00:56:46,200
So get some rest while you can.

864
00:56:46,200 --> 00:56:48,133
Good work. Get home safely.

865
00:56:48,133 --> 00:56:49,667
Yes, sir.

866
00:56:52,100 --> 00:56:54,367
But Oh Hyun Nam is something else.

867
00:56:54,367 --> 00:56:57,500
Taking a personal day
on her second day of work.

868
00:56:58,667 --> 00:57:00,900
She must've had something urgent.

869
00:57:00,900 --> 00:57:05,600
Let's let it slide this time.

870
00:57:06,700 --> 00:57:08,433
Yeah.

871
00:57:08,433 --> 00:57:09,967
Go home, everyone.

872
00:57:31,667 --> 00:57:33,024
[Honey, I've arrived. When will you get here?
Where are you, Tae Seong?]

873
00:57:35,933 --> 00:57:37,248
[New Message]

874
00:57:49,216 --> 00:57:52,600
Well, Assistant Manager Ki,
why are you still here?

875
00:57:54,600 --> 00:57:58,233
What have you been working on all day?

876
00:57:58,233 --> 00:58:02,733
I figured out
why Oh Hyun Nam joined our team.

877
00:58:04,000 --> 00:58:05,733
What are you talking about?

878
00:58:06,600 --> 00:58:07,767
Oh, Director Yoo!

879
00:58:07,767 --> 00:58:09,033
Ms. Yoo, you came just in time.

880
00:58:09,033 --> 00:58:10,600
- Oh Hyun Nam...
- Please track where this message came from.

881
00:58:10,600 --> 00:58:12,200
As fast as you can.

882
00:58:15,733 --> 00:58:20,933
What is this? What's going on?
What about Oh Hyun Nam?

883
00:58:20,933 --> 00:58:24,700
See if you can find me. But come alone.

884
00:58:24,700 --> 00:58:26,900
If you're not here before eight,
whatever happens is on you.

885
00:58:26,900 --> 00:58:28,467
It's for Bo Na.

886
00:58:30,033 --> 00:58:32,200
She came to meet her.

887
00:58:38,933 --> 00:58:40,700
What do you mean?

888
00:59:00,933 --> 00:59:04,433
[Archived Portraits]
Oh Hyun Nam. Real name, Oh Seung Ah.

889
00:59:04,433 --> 00:59:06,133
Fifteen years ago, in winter,

890
00:59:06,133 --> 00:59:09,533
Oh Seung Ah's dad, Oh Man Seok,
was released from prison.

891
00:59:09,533 --> 00:59:12,333
He went straight to see his daughter.

892
00:59:12,333 --> 00:59:14,567
That Christmas night,

893
00:59:15,967 --> 00:59:18,833
Bo Na killed Oh Seung Ah's dad.

894
00:59:19,633 --> 00:59:21,900
Right in front of her.

895
00:59:23,900 --> 00:59:25,433
So...

896
00:59:26,533 --> 00:59:29,667
Oh Hyun Nam deliberately joined Sales Team 3

897
00:59:30,433 --> 00:59:34,000
to get close to Director Yoo
and avenge her dad's death?

898
00:59:51,600 --> 00:59:55,833
Sometimes I wondered
if that day would ever come.

899
00:59:55,833 --> 00:59:58,333
That someone might find me.

900
00:59:59,333 --> 01:00:01,700
That someone might come looking for me.

901
01:00:01,700 --> 01:00:03,233
Who?

902
01:00:06,767 --> 01:00:09,067
I hope it doesn't happen.

903
01:01:16,367 --> 01:01:18,233
Where's Kwon Tae Seong?

904
01:01:19,533 --> 01:01:21,933
You ignored the photos,

905
01:01:21,933 --> 01:01:25,333
but the second I touched your husband,
you came running, huh?

906
01:01:25,333 --> 01:01:29,633
Where is he? I won't ask a third time.

907
01:01:34,867 --> 01:01:37,733
This is called Mist S.

908
01:01:39,533 --> 01:01:43,000
Drink 3 milliliters,
and in about five minutes you'll fall asleep.

909
01:01:43,000 --> 01:01:45,867
A sleep you'll never wake up from.

910
01:01:46,533 --> 01:01:49,267
I gave Kwon Tae Seong 6 milliliters.

911
01:01:53,067 --> 01:01:55,333
Have you lost your mind?

912
01:01:55,333 --> 01:01:57,200
Do you have any idea
how much that stuff costs?

913
01:01:57,200 --> 01:02:01,233
What's the price on your head?
Want in on this bill too?

914
01:02:06,167 --> 01:02:11,167
If he doesn't get the antidote
within the next hour, he'll die.

915
01:02:12,067 --> 01:02:15,800
You know exactly what that means, right?

916
01:02:20,533 --> 01:02:22,533
What do you want?

917
01:02:27,567 --> 01:02:29,500
Do you know who I am?

918
01:02:30,567 --> 01:02:32,067
I do.

919
01:02:33,433 --> 01:02:34,933
You do?

920
01:02:36,067 --> 01:02:38,967
I knew you'd figure it out.

921
01:02:40,800 --> 01:02:43,433
Or is that the work of that rude hacker?

922
01:02:45,500 --> 01:02:47,633
I know exactly who you are.

923
01:02:57,300 --> 01:02:59,700
Do you want to kill my husband?

924
01:03:09,933 --> 01:03:11,700
Then kill me too.

925
01:04:06,767 --> 01:04:08,200
Under no circumstances

926
01:04:08,200 --> 01:04:10,467
can we meet with anyone
other than the client.

927
01:04:10,467 --> 01:04:13,767
Because you messed with someone
you never should have.

928
01:04:13,767 --> 01:04:15,567
Things had been quiet for a while.

929
01:04:15,567 --> 01:04:17,067
- They said they saw Kingfisher?
- You're about to see

930
01:04:17,067 --> 01:04:18,800
another side of Kingfisher.

931
01:04:18,800 --> 01:04:20,967
You know the whole sales team workshop
is scheduled, right?

932
01:04:20,967 --> 01:04:24,200
There's a strong possibility their base
of operations is somewhere nearby.

933
01:04:24,200 --> 01:04:26,400
These punks are crossing the line.

934
01:04:26,400 --> 01:04:28,767
It's 300 million won per head!

935
01:04:28,767 --> 01:04:30,433
I think we're really going to die.

936
01:04:30,433 --> 01:04:32,800
Why isn't Mommy answering?

937
01:04:33,633 --> 01:04:35,200
Mom and Dad...

938
01:04:35,200 --> 01:04:37,033
Director Yoo is awake.

939
01:04:37,033 --> 01:04:38,100
Never lose their dignity...

940
01:04:38,100 --> 01:04:40,633
Those darn flies won't stop buzzing.

941
01:04:40,633 --> 01:04:42,700
Maybe I should go deal with them.
